.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt T150-PROBE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm probe_hid ,
.Nm probe_setreport ,
.Nm probe_ep0 ,
.Nm probe_intr
.Nd measure what macOS userspace can do to a Thrustmaster T150
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm probe_hid
.Op Fl v Ar vid
.Op Fl p Ar pid
.Op Fl o Ar dir
.Nm probe_setreport
.Op Fl v Ar vid
.Op Fl p Ar pid
.Op Fl n Ar node
.Op Fl i Ar id
.Op Fl P
.Oo
.Fl a Ar force |
.Fl A |
.Fl r Ar degrees |
.Fl g Ar gain |
.Fl x Ar bytes ...
.Oc
.Nm probe_ep0
.Op Fl v Ar vid
.Op Fl p Ar pid
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl w
.Op Fl V Ar value
.Nm probe_intr
.Op Fl v Ar vid
.Op Fl p Ar pid
.Op Fl N Ar pad
.Op Fl H Ar seconds
.Oo
.Fl I |
.Fl O |
.Fl C |
.Fl a Ar force |
.Fl A |
.Fl r Ar degrees |
.Fl g Ar gain |
.Fl R Ar seconds |
.Fl x Ar bytes ...
.Oc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These four tools answer the questions the
.Xr crossover-wheel 7
design depends on. They are measurement instruments, not part of the
finished software, and they are macOS only.
.Pp
.Nm probe_hid
inventories the HID nodes macOS publishes for the wheel. It reads properties
only and never opens a device, so it cannot disturb a running game and cannot
raise a privacy prompt. It reports the product id, which says whether the
wheel is still in boot mode, the number of nodes and their usages, the
maximum report sizes, and the full report descriptor.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v Ar vid
Match this USB vendor id. The default is 0x044f.
.It Fl p Ar pid
Also match this product id.
.It Fl o Ar dir
Write each report descriptor into
.Ar dir
as a
.Pa .bin
file for offline analysis.
.El
.Pp
.Nm probe_setreport
was the decisive experiment and it has been answered yes: it makes the wheel
physically react from an ordinary unprivileged process using
.Fn IOHIDDeviceSetReport .
The device is opened without
.Dv kIOHIDOptionsTypeSeizeDevice ,
so a running game keeps receiving input. With no action given it sets the
autocenter to full, which makes the wheel hard to turn;
.Fl a Ar 0
releases it again. That pair is the measurement.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n Ar node
Which matching HID node to write to. The default is 0.
.It Fl i Ar id
HID report id. The default is 0, meaning unnumbered. The payload never
includes the report id itself.
.It Fl P
Zero-pad the payload to the report's payload length, which is the node's
declared
.Li MaxOutputReportSize
less the report id byte that property counts and the payload does not. On this
wheel that is fourteen bytes against a declared fifteen.
.It Fl a Ar force
Set the autocenter spring to
.Ar force ,
0 to 100, and enable it.
.It Fl A
Clear the autocenter enable flag. This does
.Em not
free a held wheel, see the same option under
.Nm probe_intr .
.It Fl r Ar degrees
Set the rotation range, 270 to 1080.
.It Fl g Ar gain
Set the gain in raw hardware units, 0 to 0x80. Full scale is 0x80 and not
0xff, so 0x40 is half.
.It Fl x Ar bytes
Send a raw payload given as hex, for example
.Dq 40 11 ff 7f .
May be given up to eight times, in which case every payload is sent in order
on the same open handle. A force feedback upload needs exactly that: three
packets that the wheel correlates through slot keys, then a fourth to start
the effect, with the autocenter cleared and the gain set ahead of them.
.El
.Pp
.Nm probe_ep0
determines whether the boot to firmware vendor control transfers can be
issued, and with what privilege. It tries three escalating approaches, the
request on an unopened device, then after
.Fn USBDeviceOpen ,
then after
.Fn USBDeviceOpenSeize ,
and prints the
.Vt IOReturn
of every step. By default it performs only the read-only model query.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s
Also try
.Fn USBDeviceOpenSeize
if
.Fn USBDeviceOpen
fails. This takes the device away from every other client, including
CrossOver.
.It Fl w
Actually send the mode switch rather than only querying the model.
.It Fl V Ar value
Switch value to use with
.Fl w .
The default is 0x0006, the T150 row.
.El
.Ss probe_intr
.Nm probe_intr
writes on the interrupt OUT pipe instead of through the HID layer. The wheel
obeys both, so this is the cross-check and the reader, not the only way in.
Settings survive the release because the wheel keeps them; an effect does not,
which is what
.Fl H
is for.
Reaching that pipe means capturing the wheel away from macOS, so this tool
.Em needs root ,
unlike every other tool here. It captures, writes and hands the wheel back on
every exit path.
.Pp
With no action it sets the autocenter force to zero, which frees a wheel that
is resting on its default full autocenter. The same bytes work through
.Nm probe_setreport
without root, so this tool is the cross-check rather than the only way in.
Its packets are built by the shared encoders in
.Pa src/lib/encode.c ,
so a run exercises those too.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl N Ar pad
Zero-pad every packet to this length.
.It Fl I
Send the five initialisation packets the Linux driver sends on this pipe,
then the mode switch, in one capture. Run it on a wheel still at the boot
product id. Skipping the initialisation is what leaves the wheel blocked.
.It Fl O
Open the wheel's input,
.Dq 42 04 .
The firmware renders no effect while no application has the input open, and
nothing on macOS opens it. The open outlives this tool: it persists across
process exits and capture cycles until something sends
.Dq 42 00 ,
so close what you open, with
.Fl C
or the wheel keeps rendering whatever was last started.
.It Fl C
Close the wheel's input,
.Dq 42 00 .
.It Fl a Ar force
Autocenter to
.Ar force ,
0 to 10000, and enable it.
.Fl a Ar 0
is what frees a held wheel.
.It Fl A
Clear the autocenter enable flag. This does
.Em not
free a held wheel: the flag only says whether the autocenter survives a
process opening the wheel's input, and the effect is always active while
nothing has it open, which on macOS is always. Only the force releases it.
.It Fl r Ar degrees
Set the rotation range.
.It Fl g Ar gain
Set the gain, 0 to 10000.
.It Fl H Ar seconds
After writing, hold the wheel this long instead of handing it straight back,
reading the interrupt IN pipe while it waits. An uploaded effect does not
survive the release, because the release re-enumerates the wheel, so a force
feedback test without this cannot show anything however correct its packets
are.
.It Fl R Ar seconds
Write nothing. Read the interrupt IN pipe instead and print every report that
differs from the one before, which is how to see what the wheel puts on the
wire with nothing above the USB layer in the way. A button that produces no
line here never left the wheel. It ends with a mask of every bit that moved
at any point, which stays readable when an analogue axis jitters at rest.
.It Fl x Ar bytes
Raw hex payload, repeatable. Every packet goes out on one capture, which
matters for a sequence such as a force feedback upload, because the release
re-enumerates the wheel.
.El
.Pp
If it is killed between the capture and the release the wheel stays gone from
macOS until it is replugged. This is why the route can configure a wheel but
cannot drive effects during a game: holding the pipe means owning the device.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm probe_hid
exits 0 whenever enumeration succeeded, including when nothing matched.
.Nm probe_setreport ,
.Nm probe_ep0
and
.Nm probe_intr
exit 0 only when every operation they attempted succeeded, 1 on a device or
transfer failure, and 2 on a usage error.
.Pp
For
.Nm probe_setreport
a zero exit is necessary but not sufficient: macOS can accept a report the
firmware then ignores, so what settles the run is whether the wheel
physically moved.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Record the wheel's identity and descriptors:
.Pp
.Dl $ probe_hid -o .
.Pp
Try to make the wheel self-centre, then stop:
.Pp
.Dl $ probe_setreport
.Dl $ probe_setreport -a 0
.Pp
If that returned success but nothing moved, work through the framings:
.Pp
.Dl $ probe_setreport -i 0x0a
.Dl $ probe_setreport -P
.Dl $ probe_setreport -i 0x0a -P
.Pp
Find out whether endpoint 0 needs root:
.Pp
.Dl $ probe_ep0
.Dl $ sudo probe_ep0
.Pp
Release a wheel resting on its default autocenter, without root:
.Pp
.Dl $ probe_setreport -a 0
.Pp
The same on the interrupt OUT pipe, as a cross-check:
.Pp
.Dl $ sudo probe_intr -a 0
.Pp
See what the wheel reports while you work every control, which is how it was
shown to put all thirteen of its buttons on the wire:
.Pp
.Dl $ sudo probe_intr -R 15
.Pp
Upload an effect and give it ten seconds to do something before the wheel
goes back:
.Pp
.Dl $ sudo probe_intr -N 32 -H 10 -x \(dq02 1c ...\(dq -x \(dq41 00 41 01\(dq
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crossover-wheel 7
.Pp
The full procedure and what each outcome implies are in
.Pa docs/PROBES.md .
